1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:20,211
By eleven, the street outside the house was full of cars. Niggas came
in leather. Niggas came in silk. One arrived in a pajama shirt covered
with little white moons, a gold chain caught between the buttons.
Another still had shaving foam behind his ear. Tank looked at the
pajamas.

2
00:00:20,461 --> 00:00:42,837
"Nigga, were you asleep?" "I was participating in my relationship."
"Well, your relationship open at the bottom." The nigga buttoned
himself without slowing down. "Where she at?" "Red's got her," I said.
He stopped fixing his shirt. "Aight. What we need?" That was why I'd
called. Not because every nigga in that doorway was good.

3
00:00:43,087 --> 00:01:05,743
Some would've asked the same question at Red's house if Red had called
first. Some had carried T's coffin. Some still owed the women who
loved them an answer to a text they'd had time to read six times. But
they came. Nigga, I could work with came. The man with shaving foam
saw the broken glass. "Red do that?" "I did." "Okay.

4
00:01:05,993 --> 00:01:28,068
Nigga, I was about to get separately mad." "Stay with the original
mad. We got a deadline." He wiped his ear with his sleeve and went
inside. I watched my people fill the room. Bad decisions, borrowed
coats, guns, money trouble. A nigga I'd fought six months ago moved a
chair so Marcellus could sit more comfortably.

5
00:01:28,318 --> 00:01:49,896
Another picked up a shard of glass before Rosa stepped on it. I wanted
Shawna back. These were the niggas who had answered. The world could
interview better men in the morning. Tank stood at the dining table,
putting the three million where everybody could see it. He didn't hide
behind me. He waited until the room filled and then he spoke.

6
00:01:50,146 --> 00:02:12,513
This is the money from the motel. A few heads turned. I took it. One
man beside the piano said, Nigga, what? Tank kept his eyes on the
room. I took all of it. I let Aiden think it was gone. Red knew. He
tried to use it against him tonight. Tried? somebody asked. Tried. The
man beside the piano looked at me.

7
00:02:12,763 --> 00:02:34,605
Nigga, and this nigga still breathing? Tank's jaw moved once. I walked
between them. Look at me when you say that. The man did. Tank's
standing with me. I'm just saying— Say he stole it. He did. Say he's a
lying motherfucker. He was. Say you're gonna touch him tonight, and
you can find out how fucking fast I can forget your name.

8
00:02:34,855 --> 00:02:57,791
The room went still. Tank looked at the back of my head. I could feel
it. The man by the piano lifted his hands. Your house. Yeah. I let
that sit. My house. My money on the table. My girl with Red. If any of
that bothers you, the door already fucking broke. You ain't gotta
worry about hurting it. Nobody left.

9
00:02:58,041 --> 00:03:19,103
Rosa stood by the staircase in the borrowed coat. She watched every
face. Marcellus sat behind her with the decoy in its box and the
papers inside his jacket. The old nigga looked tired enough to
disappear if you let your eyes move too fast, but he hadn't asked to
lie down. I put my hand on the cash.

10
00:03:19,353 --> 00:03:39,256
Some of you came because you owe me. Some of you came because Red owes
you. Some of you just heard there was gonna be money. One man in the
back said, All three. I looked at him. He didn't apologize. I nodded.
Good. Nigga knows why he came. I started giving it away. Not throwing
it in the air.

11
00:03:39,506 --> 00:03:56,050
I wanted every nigga who touched it to look into my face while he did.
I wanted him to feel the weight of it and know the woman we'd left
behind had carried it out of a room full of killers before any of us
had the nerve. Stacks went into hands. Into coats.

12
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:12,556
Into the pajama shirt, where the buttons strained so hard I thought
the little moons were gonna fly off. Nigga, put that in a bag, Tank
told him. I'm good. You look pregnant. I'm good. I kept paying. Some
of them laughed. Some counted.

13
00:04:12,806 --> 00:04:31,233
One man held the money without doing either, and I remembered he'd
been sitting in a hospital hallway two nights earlier with his head in
his hands. Tonight he kissed the stack and tucked it inside his coat.
I didn't ask which part of his life I'd just bought. I had one woman
to bring home.

14
00:04:31,483 --> 00:04:54,701
The whole city could put its heart on the fucking table. When two
million had left the bags, I stopped. The last million stayed
together. I pulled the bag shut and set it aside. That's hers. Nobody
argued. Tank hadn't taken anything. I picked up a share from the two
million I'd already laid out and held it toward him. He shook his
head. No.

15
00:04:54,951 --> 00:05:15,729
Nigga, take it before I have to love you louder. Aiden. Nigga, poor
and guilty? I'm letting you have one bad feeling. Pick one. His eyes
flicked toward the men around us. Nigga, I don't want it. Then spend
it on somebody who does. I pushed the money against his chest until he
took it. He looked down at it.

16
00:05:15,979 --> 00:05:36,871
Then he put it on the table beside the million I was keeping for
Shawna. For her, he said. I left it there. I wasn't counting love back
into a fucking bag while everybody watched. Rosa came down the stairs.
And before all you niggas start singing about brotherhood, she's my
friend. Nobody laughed. They knew her.

17
00:05:37,121 --> 00:05:58,732
Half the room stood up straighter when she came close. That means if
you see her, you bring her. You don't stop to tell Red how hard you
are. You don't start explaining a grudge from 2018. You bring her. The
man with shaving foam behind his ear nodded. We got you, Rosa. No,
baby. You better have her. She turned to me.

18
00:05:58,982 --> 00:06:17,980
I had held back part of the two million for her. I pushed it across
the table. She stared at it. What's this? Yours. For what? Whatever
you want. Her face went tight. You paying me to stay home? I'm paying
you because she loves you. Rosa looked up. Nigga, don't do that right
now.

19
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:40,280
She gets out of that car tonight, I want somebody here she knew before
every room had me in it. For the first time since she'd walked through
the broken door, Rosa looked her age and her fear at once. Thirty-four
years old, tired, one earring gone, holding the coat closed with a
hand that had finally stopped shaking. You bring her, she said.

20
00:06:40,530 --> 00:07:03,414
I nodded. She slapped my face. Not hard enough to knock me down. Hard
enough that the room went silent. With your mouth, Aiden. I swallowed.
I'm bringing her. She kissed the same cheek. Then go, baby. I turned
to the room. Any of you niggas here think Red owns Vegas? Fuck Red,
somebody said. Anybody think that nigga owns my wife?

21
00:07:03,664 --> 00:07:23,779
Rosa made a sound behind me. I turned halfway. What? You ask her yet?
I'm going to. Then quit inviting these niggas before me. The room
broke open. Men laughed, slapped each other's shoulders, called out
shit about weddings and suits and who wasn't allowed near an open bar.
I let them.

22
00:07:24,029 --> 00:07:45,404
For a few seconds we had a future big enough to crowd a room. Then I
raised my hand. Niggas, listen to me. They quieted. I ain't asking you
to die because I fell in love. I'm asking you to stand up with me
because that nigga thinks he can take anything he sees. He took a
man's wife. Took another man's diamond.

23
00:07:45,654 --> 00:08:09,175
Took Dante out to the desert and left him there. Tonight he took
Shawna. I put my hand over the cross. He keeps telling everybody I'm
wearing a dead nigga's jewelry. Fine. Let him look at it while I come
get my girl. Tank stepped beside me. Ten toes, he said. The room
answered. Down. He said it again, louder. Ten toes. Down.

24
00:08:09,425 --> 00:08:29,487
Nigga, the windows shook. The broken front door moved in its frame.
For one wild second I wanted the whole city to hear us, every
penthouse and every parking lot and every woman waiting for a man to
come back different. I kissed the cross. Then I went outside. Tank
drove the Mercedes.

25
00:08:29,737 --> 00:08:49,115
I sat beside him because I still couldn't lean back without feeling
T's bullet and because if anybody was going to meet Red first, it was
going to be me. Marcellus got into the back. I looked over my
shoulder. You sure about this? No. Nigga, you can wait with Rosa. I
have waited enough.

26
00:08:49,365 --> 00:09:07,293
He shut the door before I could offer him anything else. The decoy sat
in its box beside him. The letters and the papers were in his coat. My
phone lay faceup on my knee. Rosa stood in the driveway with the money
she hadn't bothered to pick up still inside the house.

27
00:09:07,543 --> 00:09:27,947
Tank had put the bag with Shawna's million and his returned share in
the back. Red had asked for three million. He was getting what was
left after I'd paid the niggas coming to take his kingdom. She came to
my window. Aiden. I looked at her. She likes gardenias. What? For the
wedding. She likes gardenias.

28
00:09:28,197 --> 00:09:47,306
And she will lie and tell you roses because men always buy roses. I
gripped the door. Gardenias. And don't let that old man give her away.
I'll do it. Marcellus said, I hadn't volunteered. Rosa pointed at him
through the glass. Keep it that way. She stepped back.

29
00:09:47,556 --> 00:10:08,212
The cars pulled out behind us until the street looked like the city
had emptied its garages for a funeral and nobody had agreed whose.
Thirty engines. Maybe more by the time we reached the highway. Rex
Crown came in a black coupe; Little Saint rode beside him. Mercedes
and Porsche took the green Bentley.

30
00:10:08,462 --> 00:10:31,155
Bell had brought my police Lamborghini back, and Knox rode with her at
the head of the convoy. Headlights filled both mirrors. My niggas had
come wearing their money and their worst intentions, and I loved every
last one of them for showing up. Tank kept both hands on the wheel.
After a while he said, You should let the doctor look at you after.

31
00:10:31,405 --> 00:10:55,122
After. I'm saying. I heard you. He nodded. The lights thinned outside
the windows. Vegas went from towers to signs to little burning squares
behind us. Ahead was black desert and the road laid through it. Tank.
Yeah. When you came back for the money. Did he look like himself? He
knew who I meant. He drove another few seconds before he answered. No.

32
00:10:55,372 --> 00:11:17,656
I looked down at the cross. Good. Tank's hands tightened. You don't
gotta say that. I know. He didn't answer. I watched the side of his
face and remembered him standing behind T in the parking lot, as big
as a wall, waiting for somebody else to decide what he'd do. I'm glad
you here. His jaw moved. Yeah. Don't make me say it twice.

33
00:11:17,906 --> 00:11:40,384
I heard you. In the back, Marcellus turned the decoy's box between his
hands. She wore blue the last time I took her dancing, he said.
Neither of us asked who. Celeste. I was late. She was furious. By the
time I got there, she'd danced with three other men. Three? I said.
She counted them for me. Tank glanced in the mirror.

34
00:11:40,634 --> 00:12:02,878
You do something to those niggas? I asked for the fourth dance. I
looked out at the dark. Could've been me. It wasn't. He closed the box
and rested his head against the seat. We drove the rest of that
stretch without talking. At eleven fifty-four, Red called. I put him
on speaker. You coming? he asked. You hear the cars?

35
00:12:03,128 --> 00:12:24,139
I told you to come ready to apologize. I am. Tank looked at me. I told
her I'd never let you put your hands on her again. Got a lot to
apologize for. Red breathed into the phone. You think all those niggas
love you? Enough to leave the house. That's money. Then you should've
paid better. He went quiet.

36
00:12:24,388 --> 00:12:43,841
I heard Shawna in the background. I couldn't make out the words, only
her voice and the way he moved the phone away from her. Let me talk to
her. You'll see her soon. Nigga, let me— He hung up. I gripped the
phone so hard Tank reached over and took it before I broke that too.
We're here, he said.

37
00:12:44,091 --> 00:13:08,817
The casino rose out of the desert half finished, huge and white under
lights that made the empty windows look blacker. Red had built columns
tall enough for a king and stopped before anybody could decide what
kingdom he thought he had. Plastic sheeting moved behind the glass. A
fountain outside had never held water. Cars waited across the
entrance. Men stood between them.

38
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:28,558
Above the front doors, a balcony ran along the second floor beneath an
unfinished crown of stone. There she was. Shawna stood at the railing
in Rosa's ruined dress. Her hair blew across her face. Even from the
car I could see Dante's watch on her wrist. Red stood beside her.

39
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:50,841
He lifted the hand with the ring and waved like he'd invited us for
dinner. Behind me, engine after engine went quiet. My niggas were
here. I opened my door. My side hurt. My hand hurt. Everything in me
that knew how to be scared was awake and screaming. I put both feet on
the ground anyway. Shawna saw me.

40
00:13:51,091 --> 00:14:15,402
She stepped toward the railing before Red caught her arm. Aiden! I
looked straight up at her. I'm here, baby. The clock on my phone
turned eleven fifty-nine. The first roadblock waited beyond the last
gas station. Two trucks across the highway. Men beside them. No
uniforms. No lights except the white glare of their headlights pointed
into our faces.

41
00:14:15,652 --> 00:14:34,815
A line of barrels burned between the trucks, and behind the flames I
could see the same kind of patience Red had worn across the breakfast
table. Tank slowed. Behind us thirty engines changed their voices at
once. My phone rang. Knox. "I see them," she said.

42
00:14:35,065 --> 00:14:53,662
"Stay in the convoy." "Nigga, the convoy is me." "Then don't make me
explain to your wife why you turned into a road accident before you
got there." A shot hit the Mercedes hood. Tank pulled left. Another
struck the windshield and made a white star directly in front of him.

43
00:14:53,912 --> 00:15:20,109
Marcellus dropped in the back, his coat closed over the letters and
the decoy like the old nigga had decided history could wait below the
window line. Knox's police Lamborghini came out beside us. Officer
Bell was driving; the chief leaned forward in the passenger seat,
looking at the roadblock like somebody had finally annoyed her enough
to deserve the whole department. The siren rose.

44
00:15:20,359 --> 00:15:42,682
One of the men by the truck stepped backward. Another raised his gun
anyway. "Hardheaded nigga," I said. Tank put his foot down. We left
the road in a sheet of dust. The Mercedes bounced across the shoulder,
hit a shallow ditch, and came up with its engine still screaming. My
head struck the roof. I tasted blood.

45
00:15:42,932 --> 00:16:02,442
Behind us the convoy divided, cars sweeping wide through the desert
while shots flashed between the trucks. The men had expected a line.
They got a fucking horizon. Rex's black coupe came past on our right.
Little Saint rode beside it on a new motorcycle with no paint on the
tank.

46
00:16:02,692 --> 00:16:26,393
He'd borrowed it from a man who apparently understood lending
something to my nigga meant accepting an interesting return policy.
Mercedes and Porsche came through the dust in the green Bentley.
Porsche had the roof down. Mercedes held her hair away from her face
with one hand and a pistol in the other. "Keep the old man down!" she
shouted as they passed.

47
00:16:26,643 --> 00:16:48,741
"Old man is down," Marcellus said from the back seat. "The old man is
thoroughly fucking down." I couldn't help it. I laughed. Nigga, I
laughed with a bullet hole in my windshield and the woman I loved
waiting inside a nightmare, because that old man had come through
eight years of prison and still knew when my friends needed
correcting.

48
00:16:48,991 --> 00:17:12,115
The first truck started moving. Its driver turned toward the desert to
cut off the cars passing on that side. Rex braked hard. Little Saint
swerved clear. The truck's huge front wheel climbed the edge of a
ditch, and for a second the whole thing leaned toward the coupe. I saw
Rex looking up through his windshield. I saw Little Saint turn back.

49
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:36,513
"Tank." "I see." "Nigga, this time I believe you." Tank drove the
Mercedes straight into the truck's rear corner. Metal struck metal.
The car jumped sideways. My shoulder hit the door, and every stitch in
my side tried to leave without me. The truck's rear swung away from
Rex, its wheels clawing at loose dirt. It rolled far enough that the
coupe could get clear.

50
00:17:36,763 --> 00:17:55,079
Little Saint rode through the gap beside it and came out raising one
fist. "Aiden!" "Tank!" I shouted back. The big nigga glanced at me.
"What?" "I'm giving you your fucking credit. Enjoy it." He grinned
despite the blood on his lip. The truck stopped against a low rise.

51
00:17:55,329 --> 00:18:17,222
Its driver jumped out, took one look at the number of cars now
surrounding him, and dropped the gun he'd brought down from the cab.
Bell and Knox reached him first. The chief got out with her weapon
raised. "You blocked my captain's road." The man stared at the gold on
her uniform. "Your captain?" She pointed toward me through the dust.

52
00:18:17,472 --> 00:18:40,355
"That one." He looked. His face fell so completely I almost respected
the honesty of it. "They didn't say it was him." "Nigga," I shouted
from the window, "what part of thirty cars looked like a small
mistake?" Rex pulled beside us with his window down. His eyebrow was
still bleeding where the gala guard had hit him. He looked at Tank,
then at me.

53
00:18:40,605 --> 00:19:01,384
"Three times." "That one was Tank." "Then I owe the family." Tank
lifted two fingers off the wheel. The nigga didn't even try to look
modest. I'd have been angry if he had. Behind us, Knox's officers took
the men off the road. The second truck's crew had run before the first
one stopped moving.

54
00:19:01,634 --> 00:19:24,023
I could see their flashlights bouncing through the distance, four
little dots trying to become somebody else's fucking problem. The
convoy found the highway again. Thirty engines. A few more scratched.
A few more loud. Nobody missing. The police Lamborghini took the front
while Knox's remaining cruisers held the road behind us.

55
00:19:24,273 --> 00:19:46,948
Bell gave the siren one short burst, and the cars answered with their
horns. Marcellus sat up carefully in the back. "Are we finished doing
that?" "For now." "Good. My tie has given up." I reached back and
straightened it for him at the next slow bend. "Nigga, you meeting
forty million dollars. Look ready." He looked at me, then down at the
cross.

56
00:19:47,198 --> 00:20:12,210
"Damn, boy," he said. I smiled. "Magnificent." The old man nodded as
if he'd completed the last repair the evening required. At eleven
fifty-nine, the unfinished casino rose out of the desert in front of
us. Lights burned behind its empty windows. Our headlights spread
across the parking lot until every naked wall had a shadow of my
people on it.

57
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:23,312
I saw blue on a balcony. Shawna. My whole fucking body knew before my
eyes finished the distance. Tank stopped the Mercedes. I opened the
door.
